              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "EILISH40"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a tasty salad (especially on a hot summer's day) as it stands, but adding some crumbled feta really livens up the taste. This is not a salad to be overlooked and also easy on your diet!!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Teresa Steen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We liked it ok the first time. The second time I added diced jicama, left out the the sugar and vinegar and only salted the cucumber for an hour over a colander. Refrigerator for several hours, served with feta cheese and fresh ground black pepper. Outstanding!",
            "datePublished": "2024-06-28T23:31:59.530Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "James"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wonderfully simple and delicious. I salted my sliced and seeded cucumbers with thinly sliced red onions, letting them drain in the sink in a colander. This drained excess liquid and added crispness to the cucumber and onions. I used homemade Mulberry Vinegar made on my ranch instead of Italian Basalmic. Just delicious and everyone raved on the symphony of flavors.",
            "datePublished": "2026-07-20T22:25:24.338Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Elizabeth Laming-Lessard"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a wonderful recipe. I let it sit for a few hours in the fridge and the flavors blended to perfection. A bit salty and a bit sweet. I let the cukes sit in the balsamic vinegar before adding to the watermelon.",
            "datePublished": "2011-08-02T07:54:59.953Z"
          },
          {
